On Apr 19, 9:35 am, MainiacJoe <mainiac...@gmail.com> wrote:

> My question, then, is whether I'm better off focusing on dagger
> initially and saving my initial orcish (or elven) arrows until I
> can stop them from evaporating, or focusing on bow initially and
> hoping to replace my racial arrows later.

In the early game, do whatever makes it easiest to survive the next
hundred turns or so.

Personally, if I were playing as a ranger and could find a pretty
good stack of daggers, I'd probably mostly use those.  Daggers don't
vanish when you throw them, and Rangers can advance clear up to
expert in the dagger skill, and, more important than either of those
considerations IMO, you can throw daggers while wielding a melee
weapon, so you don't have to waste turns switching from your melee
weapon to a bow every time you want to shoot something only to turn
around two turns later and waste *another* turn switching back when
the monster closes to melee range.  But this is at least partly a
matter of personal playing style.  If you find that using the bow
lets you kill things more easily in the early game, by all means,
use it.

Don't worry about whether you'll have the ideal weapon in the late
game.  If you make it to the late game, your ability to survive
will be MUCH higher than in the early game.  In the late game
you'll probably be able to sacrifice and get your longsword skill
unrestricted, then enchant one up to +6 if not +7.  In the late
game you won't need projectile weapons nearly as badly, because
you'll have speed boots and attack wands and controlled teleport
and very likely some useful combat spells as well.  You'll also
have a ton of food in the late game (all those C- and K-rations
the soldiers drop), so if you feel like it you can just hang out
in the Gnomish Mines for a few thousand turns and kill orcs (and
whatever else shows up) until you find any weapon you happen to
want (as long as its probability of showing up in monster inventory
or as a death drop is even slightly above zero).  But you almost
certainly won't *need* to do that, because in the late game your
level and skill and strength and whatnot will all be so high that
the racial bonus won't be very important anyway.  The late game can
take care of itself.  Don't worry about it.  Worry about surviving
long enough to GET to the late game.


